# Skeleton Loading Patterns in React/Next.js

## Overview

Skeleton screens are placeholder UI elements that mimic the layout of content while it loads. They prevent layout shifts by reserving the exact space the final content will occupy.

## Core Principles

1. **Match dimensions exactly**: The skeleton must occupy the same space as the final content
2. **Reflect structure**: Mimic the layout structure (headers, text blocks, images)
3. **Use animation**: `animate-pulse` or shimmer effects indicate loading
4. **No conditional removal of containers**: The outer container should always render; only the inner content should swap between skeleton and real content

## Tailwind CSS Skeleton Components

### Image Placeholder

```tsx
<div className="w-full h-48 bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
```

### Text Line Placeholder

```tsx
<div className="h-4 w-3/4 bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
```

### Card Skeleton

```tsx
function CardSkeleton() {
  return (
    <div className="bg-white rounded-lg p-4 shadow">
      <div className="w-full h-48 bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
      <div className="mt-3 h-4 w-3/4 bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
      <div className="mt-2 h-4 w-1/4 bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
      <div className="mt-3 h-10 w-full bg-gray-300 animate-pulse rounded" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Grid of Skeletons

```tsx
function ProductGridSkeleton({ count = 15 }: { count?: number }) {
  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      {Array.from({ length: count }).map((_, i) => (
        <CardSkeleton key={i} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Pattern: Container Always Renders

```tsx
// GOOD: Container always rendered, only content swaps
function Sidebar({ data, loading }) {
  return (
    <aside className="w-[220px] shrink-0 p-5">
      {loading ? <SidebarSkeleton /> : <SidebarContent data={data} />}
    </aside>
  );
}

// BAD: Container conditionally rendered, causes shift
function Sidebar({ data }) {
  if (!data) return null;  // This causes layout shift!
  return <aside className="w-[220px]">...</aside>;
}
```

## Pattern: Banner Placeholder

```tsx
function Banner({ text, loading }) {
  if (loading) {
    return (
      <div className="py-24 px-4 bg-gray-200 animate-pulse">
        <div className="h-8 w-1/3 mx-auto bg-gray-300 rounded" />
      </div>
    );
  }
  return (
    <div className="py-24 px-4 bg-blue-500 text-white text-center font-bold text-2xl">
      {text}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Integration with Data Fetching

```tsx
function Component() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/api/data')
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(data => {
        setData(data);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []);

  return (
    <div className="fixed-dimensions-container">
      {loading ? <Skeleton /> : <RealContent data={data} />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

The key insight: the outer container with fixed dimensions should ALWAYS render. Only the inner content swaps.

